{"4522140": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Bloodweight", "steam_appid": 4522140, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" > the weight of blood.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >every bloodline begins as a single name pressed into wet ink. you carry it</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >for as long as it lasts — and it will not last.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >each generation deals you ONE HEIR: their genome, their temperament, the</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >realm's pressures faction by faction, and the chronicle the last hand left</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >behind. you spend their life. then the page turns to the next.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >one hundred generations. one ledger. the Soul Teller writes down everything</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >you do.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >▸ BREED</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >every heir is a knot of inherited tissue and inherited temperament — body,</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >mind, word, hand. read them the way the chronicler does: not as numbers, but</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >as a hand the family is dealt and forced to play.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >▸ DECIDE</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >the witan convenes. events strike without warning. the crucible tests the</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >blood. you make the call, the ledger logs it, and every choice compounds</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >down the generations.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >▸ READ</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >turn the page and read your house like a book — the heir illuminated, the</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >chronicler's account of the age, the running weight of power, wealth, and the</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >blood's own dream. a saga you don't watch so much as witness.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >▸ END</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >bloodlines fail. when yours does — and it will — the Soul Teller sets down the</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >whole run in unsparing prose. there is no clean ending it leaves out. you will</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >read about yourself.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >▸ PROC GENESIS</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >procedural everything: heirs, faces, names, events, factions, eras, mutation</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >pressure, cultural memory — and the prose itself. no two ledgers read the same.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >when one line closes, the page opens for the next.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >so — when the Soul Teller finally reads your story back to you... what will</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >it say?</p>", "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" > the weight of blood.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >every bloodline begins as a single name pressed into wet ink. you carry it</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >for as long as it lasts — and it will not last.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >each generation deals you ONE HEIR: their genome, their temperament, the</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >realm's pressures faction by faction, and the chronicle the last hand left</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >behind. you spend their life. then the page turns to the next.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >one hundred generations. one ledger. the Soul Teller writes down everything</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >you do.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >▸ BREED</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >every heir is a knot of inherited tissue and inherited temperament — body,</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >mind, word, hand. read them the way the chronicler does: not as numbers, but</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >as a hand the family is dealt and forced to play.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >▸ DECIDE</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >the witan convenes. events strike without warning. the crucible tests the</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >blood. you make the call, the ledger logs it, and every choice compounds</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >down the generations.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >▸ READ</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >turn the page and read your house like a book — the heir illuminated, the</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >chronicler's account of the age, the running weight of power, wealth, and the</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >blood's own dream. a saga you don't watch so much as witness.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >▸ END</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >bloodlines fail. when yours does — and it will — the Soul Teller sets down the</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >whole run in unsparing prose. there is no clean ending it leaves out. you will</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >read about yourself.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >▸ PROC GENESIS</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >procedural everything: heirs, faces, names, events, factions, eras, mutation</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >pressure, cultural memory — and the prose itself. no two ledgers read the same.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >when one line closes, the page opens for the next.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >so — when the Soul Teller finally reads your story back to you... what will</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >it say?</p>", "short_description": "100 generations. one ledger. one heir at a time. you are the bloodline itself, guiding your lineage through the ages. you spend each life; the Soul Teller writes what it was. when your line ends, you read the chronicle of yourself. how will YOUR dynasty fall?", "supported_languages": "English", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4522140/227172420c9958f5770b0b0a43f8c9b4a8affeaa/header.jpg?t=1784131300", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4522140/64132490916eed4451d2c04053fe092ba005e2ba/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1784131300", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4522140/64132490916eed4451d2c04053fe092ba005e2ba/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1784131300", "website": "https://bloodweight.com/", "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operat